{{!-- The players' view of a route the GM has shown them (dialogs/SharedRouteWindow.js): the line,
      where they set out, where they are bound and the stops on the way, over one regional map.
      Its context is the thinned map object from utils/shared-route.js `sharedRouteView`.

      NOTHING HERE IS A CONTROL. The GM's pin layer (expedition-journey-pins.hbs) is a planner, and
      every pin on it is a button; this is a picture of the answer, so the marks are plain spans
      that take no pointer events and the reader can drag the map from anywhere on it. They carry
      no `data-slug` or `data-tier`, which is also what tells the zoom window's pan handler they are
      scenery rather than something to click.

      HIDDEN FROM A SCREEN READER as a whole, because the window says all of it in words: the total
      and the legs are written out beside the map, and the picture's own alt text names the map and
      the two ends of the way. Reading these labels as well would say the same journey twice.

      NAMES ONLY, no times: the leg list carries the times, and a pin's time is the table's time to
      that one place, which on a drawn way need not be the total the list adds up to. --}}
<div class="stonetop-shared-route-layer" aria-hidden="true">
{{> "stonetop.expedition-journey-line" this}}

{{#each this.spots}}
<span style="left:{{this.left}}%;top:{{this.top}}%"
      class="stonetop-journey-pick stonetop-journey-spot h-{{this.anchorH}} v-{{this.anchorV}}{{#if this.isOrigin}} is-origin{{/if}}{{#if this.isStop}} is-stop{{/if}}{{#if this.isChosen}} is-chosen{{/if}}">
  <span class="stonetop-journey-dot"></span>
  <span class="stonetop-journey-tag">{{this.name}}</span>
</span>
{{/each}}

{{#if this.start}}
<span class="stonetop-journey-pick stonetop-journey-start h-{{this.start.anchorH}} v-{{this.start.anchorV}}"
      style="left:{{this.start.left}}%;top:{{this.start.top}}%">
  <span class="stonetop-journey-dot"></span>
  <span class="stonetop-journey-tag">{{this.start.label}}</span>
</span>
{{/if}}

{{#each this.exits}}
<span style="left:{{this.left}}%;top:{{this.top}}%"
      class="stonetop-journey-pick stonetop-journey-exit h-{{this.anchorH}} v-{{this.anchorV}}{{#if this.isStop}} is-stop{{/if}}{{#if this.isChosen}} is-chosen{{/if}}">
  <span class="stonetop-journey-arrow"><i class="fas fa-angles-right"></i></span>
  <span class="stonetop-journey-tag">{{this.label}}</span>
</span>
{{/each}}

{{#each this.marks}}
<span class="stonetop-journey-mark{{#if this.isEnd}} is-end{{/if}}"
      style="left:{{this.left}}%;top:{{this.top}}%">{{this.mark}}</span>
{{/each}}
</div>
